## Phase 3: Firestore Sync for isFavorite

Goal: Ensure favorite status syncs between local and cloud.

- [ ] Task: Write failing tests for sync
  - Test push includes `is_favorite` field
  - Test pull reads `is_favorite` from Firestore
- [ ] Task: Update `CloudNote` model in [lib/services/cloud/cloud_note.dart](file:///d:/gemini_cli/Notely/lib/services/cloud/cloud_note.dart)
  - Add `isFavorite` field
- [ ] Task: Update [lib/services/cloud/firebase_cloud_storage.dart](file:///d:/gemini_cli/Notely/lib/services/cloud/firebase_cloud_storage.dart)
  - Include `is_favorite` in document writes/reads
- [ ] Task: Update [lib/services/sync/sync_service.dart](file:///d:/gemini_cli/Notely/lib/services/sync/sync_service.dart)
  - Map `is_favorite` in push and pull operations
- [ ] Task: Run tests — verify all pass
- [ ] **Acceptance**: Create favorited note → syncs to Firestore → pull shows correct flag

---

## Phase 4: Repository Layer Extensions

Goal: Expose favorites and search via repository with proper testing.

- [ ] Task: Write failing tests for repository methods
  - Test `toggleFavorite(id)` updates flag and marks dirty
  - Test `favoriteNotes` stream filters correctly
  - Test `searchNotes(query)` returns matching notes
- [ ] Task: Implement in [lib/services/repository/note_repository.dart](file:///d:/gemini_cli/Notely/lib/services/repository/note_repository.dart)
  - `toggleFavorite(String id)` → update sqflite, mark sync dirty
  - `Stream<List<DatabaseNote>> get favoriteNotes` → filtered stream
  - `searchNotes(String query)` → filter by content JSON
- [ ] Task: Run tests — verify all pass
- [ ] **Acceptance**: Toggle persists, streams filter correctly, search returns matches

